Test-first guard, actually enforcing — 2026-10-17
Host: Darwin 24.6.0 x86_64, pytest 9.1.1, tdd-guard-pytest 0.1.2, tdd-guard 1.7.0

-- What was missing
   The guard reads test state from a reporter. This project had none, so
   .claude/tdd-guard/data held only modifications.json and every implementation
   edit was allowed. Installed and authenticated was not the same as enforcing.

-- What was added
   .venv (uv, Python 3.14.7) with pytest and tdd-guard-pytest; pyproject.toml
   pointing pytest at Test/. The suite itself is untouched plain unittest, and
   .apex/verify.json still runs it through 'python3 -m unittest'.
   Run it for the guard with: .venv/bin/python -m pytest

-- Three latent test bugs this exposed
   sys.executable under pytest is .venv/bin/python, whose path contains a space
   ('Apex Engineering'). Three places built a command from it without quoting and
   had only ever run under space-free interpreters:
     test_verify_hook.py   verify.json command, run with shell=True   -> shlex.quote
     test_apex_project.py  verify command, run with shell=True        -> shlex.quote
     test_coding_bridge.py '#!' shebang, which cannot hold a space    -> /bin/sh wrapper
   15 tests failed under pytest before the fixes; the bugs were in the tests.

-- Reporter output
   .claude/tdd-guard/data/test.json now written: 10 test modules

-- Measured decisions, with test results present
   Edit a constant while every test passes          -> allowed  (a green-state change)
   Write a test file adding one failing test        -> allowed
   Write a new implementation file with real logic  -> BLOCKED
     "Premature implementation ... there is no test output provided to justify it.
      There is no evidence of a failing test that required this code."

-- Both runners agree: 116 pass under pytest, 116 pass under unittest.
